// C++-interop coverage: CLASS and FUNCTION TEMPLATES, and std:: specializations.
// The plain C++ surface is in Test/test_cpp_interop.cb; the CFlat bridge (CFlat-defined
// [cpp] structs and reverse callbacks) is in Test/test_cpp_interop_bridge.cb.

// The libc++ checks below call members that carry no noexcept specification. Following
// clang, such calls are allowed by default (an escaping exception terminates the program);
// Test/errors/err_cpp_template_may_throw.cb proves the opt-in --cpp-strict-noexcept gate.
// End-to-end C++-interop coverage. Each section exercises one path of the C++ interop
// pipeline; on failure the section's exit code identifies which one regressed.
//   C++ CLASS TEMPLATES instantiated from CFlat - `cppt.Box<int>` and `cppt.Box<double>`
//     from one header-only pattern (constructor, get/set, operator[] bound to the index
//     expression, operator==), a per-specialization static counter, a specialization over a
//     nontrivial C++ class whose DEFAULTED destructor still has to run, and the same
//     specialization named in two functions (one registration, one symbol).
//   libc++ through the same path - std.vector<int>, std.vector<double>, std.string, and the
//     nested std.vector<std.string>, plus element destruction counted for
//     std.vector<cppi.Tracked>.
//   A specialization whose element type is a POINTER (std.vector<char*>), where every member
//     signature that names the container itself carries an inner '*' that the type mapper
//     must not strip, and a `move` argument to a libc++ member.
//   C++ lazy aliases, unnamed nested enums, nullptr defaults, exact constructor ranking, and
//     member signatures that request nested std::string specializations.
//   C++ function-template deduction wrappers for free functions, static and instance
//     members, class returns, string literals, and explicit type arguments.
//   C++ brace-list arguments through initializer_list, a class constructor from a brace
//     list, a class parameter, and an explicit function-template specialization.
//   Dependent function-pointer ABI types in an uninstantiated template.
//   C++ header-walk implicit and defaulted special members - local destruction, copy/move
//     construction, and a defaulted destructor.
//   C++ rvalue receiver lifetime handoff, bool bitfield packing, and inherited constructors
//     forwarded through operator->.
//   Constructors declared over DEPENDENT typedefs (the c10::IListRef shape): clang only
//     offers the dependent pattern, which the extractor now retains so the class is still
//     constructible.
//   C++ member default wrappers with a leading long literal, comparing optional and plain
//     trailing parameters.
//   A variadic constructor template called with named LOCALS in the `T x = T(a, b)`
//     declaration form (the torch::nn::Sequential shape).
//   A refused member with a default-argument wrapper retries once its class-typed parameter
//     is registered, at full and reduced arity.
//   std.atomic<T> members, whose libc++ shape declares each one twice - a `volatile` overload
//     and a non-volatile one - that collapse onto a single CFlat signature, plus the same shape
//     replicated in atmrep (Test/library/cpp_interop_tpl.h) so the coverage is version-proof.
//   Public fields of a requested class-template specialization remain addressable through a
//     specialization alias, even beside a same-named namespace.
//   An inferred unique_ptr returned from a C++ loader-shaped function moves its nontrivial
//     sret result, including a by-value Dataset and a defaulted size_t-converting options
//     class.
//   A namespace-scope C++ alias whose default template argument canonicalizes differently
//     still names the vector element identity.
//   An inherited CRTP member template with a dependent return type and a transform that has
//     only an implicit default constructor.
//   Canonical spelling of a dependent CRTP member-template return whose template argument is
//     a namespace-local alias, plus retrying a by-value transform apply_batch after its
//     vector element is registered.
//   Homogeneous C++ class brace arguments materialized as contiguous copies/moves for
//     std::vector and pointer-pair SpanOf parameters.
//   auto locals move-construct nontrivial C++ sret returns before the temporary is nulled,
//     both directly and through operator-> forwarding.
//   Namespace-scope C++ using-directives resolve free functions, types, and function
//     templates through a lookup-time namespace fallback.
//   A nontrivial C++ class built from `call() * s` and `(a + s) * t` moves the outermost
//     operator result into the local; temporaries destroyed.
//   NON-TYPE template arguments on C++ function templates - `cppt.nth_of<0>(v)`,
//     `box.slot<3>()`, mixed `cppt.scaled<3, int>(5)`, and `std.get<0>/<1>` on a std::tuple
//     returned by value.
//   Members inherited from a class-template-specialization base - a CRTP
//     NormBase<D, Derived> whose members only get a body when the specialization is ODR-used,
//     reached from plain derived classes and through a holder's operator->.
//   Namespace-scope C++ constexpr variables retain their qualified names and declared
//     enum/bool/integer types as compile-time constants.
//   C++ constructor temporaries are receivers for member calls, chained member calls, fields,
//     declaration initializers, and const-reference args.
//   Nested std::tuple returns through auto and explicit locals, nested std.get calls, a
//     defaulted optional tuple parameter, and RAII cleanup.
//   C++ string literals and foreign class values use converting constructors at by-value
//     call arguments; chained calls preserve references and destroy argument temporaries
//     exactly once.
//   Sibling class-template-specialization bases keep their own layout, inherited members,
//     operator->, and inherited constructors.
//   Brace overloads at parameter indices 1 and 2, defaulted and explicit options, and
//     derived-to-base references/pointers through a two-level public hierarchy with a
//     non-primary base and virtual dispatch.
//   A class-template specialization's nested Item keeps the enclosing specialization identity
//     for reference-returning operator[] and front(), including two specializations in one
//     function and a nontrivial value type.
//   Heterogeneous C++ brace elements convert into one initializer_list element class,
//     including a namespace-level using-directive re-export and destruction of the
//     materialized nontrivial elements.
//   Namespace-scope floating constexpr values retain float/double types, long double narrows
//     to CFlat double, and all values remain usable in arithmetic, comparisons, and C++
//     function arguments.
//   Nontrivial C++ class declaration locals initialized from call/call and
//     constructor/constructor ternaries, with both branch outcomes and live-count cleanup; a
//     ternary of temporaries as a call argument.
//   A parenthesized ternary used as the condition of a class-declaration ternary, with both
//     outcomes and live-count cleanup.
//   Named lvalues in class brace lists stay intact, brace temporaries are destroyed per full
//     expression in a loop, converting constructors balance by-value and local
//     materialization, and T(args) works for a no-standard-include aggregate with
//     two-argument initialization.
//   One shared C++ foreign identity for positive/negative non-type template bases and
//     unsigned-char ArrayRef-like bases, including inherited members and derived-to-base
//     free-function conversions.
//   Canonical C++ primitive identities for unsigned long, size_t, unsigned, long double, and
//     a std::vector<size_t>-style round trip.
//   A class-template specialization named through a GLOBAL-scope C++ alias or typedef - both
//     spellings reach one record.
//   A CLASS-typed subscript index - a named std.string lvalue as a std.map key (incremented
//     twice, and not moved from), the same key through find/count, a struct field and a
//     dereferenced pointer as keys, a user-header C++ class key, and a CFlat-native
//     operator[] whose index parameter is a struct.
//   C++ member ref-qualifiers preserve lvalue/rvalue receiver selection for assignment,
//     fields, dereferences, elements, calls, temporaries, explicit move, and null-conditional
//     forwarding.
//   A CFlat string LITERAL as the operand of a C++ operator - it is the 'char*' it lowers to,
//     not a CFlat 'string', so it binds 'operator+=(const char*)' on std.string and on a user
//     class, picks the char* leg over the std::string one, reaches a free operator on either
//     side of the class operand, and still refuses a 'char' parameter
//     (Test/errors/err_cpp_string_literal_operator_char.cb). The char* local, std.map literal
//     key, char literal and CFlat-native string legs are controls that behaved identically
//     before the fix.
//   A C++ namespace whose declarations ALL name a std:: specialization (parameter, return by
//     value, nested namespace) is registered even though binding those signatures is deferred
//     to first use; nsstd_mix is the control that one std-free declaration already registered.
//   Qualified C++ class-template constructor temporaries in CFlat call arguments, C++
//     free/member calls, returns, assignment RHS, zero/two-argument constructors, nested
//     specializations, and user types.
//   STATIC members of a C++ class TEMPLATE reached through the qualified specialization
//     spelling - static methods with 0/1/2 arguments, a static data member read and written, a
//     static constexpr member, specializations over a primitive, a user C++ class and another
//     specialization, the call in statement / argument / condition position, a specialization
//     instantiated ONLY by the static call, and the spelling inside a CFlat generic body.
//   Ordinary free functions requested on demand from direct standard headers: sort,
//     make_shared, string conversion/parsing, C-library overloads, numeric algorithms,
//     make_pair, and nested chrono/thread APIs.
//   A std container whose element is a std specialization over a USER class -
//     vector<vector<Cell>>, vector<shared_ptr<Cell>>, both map positions, three levels deep,
//     and a map naming classes from TWO user headers. The request must union the owning group
//     of every class nested at any depth, not just the outer template's; each of these was
//     refused with "no imported C++ header declares 'std::vector'".
//     Test/errors/err_cpp_nested_missing.cb pins the diagnostic for an argument that genuinely
//     is not declared.
//   The `iterator -> const_iterator` conversion at an OVERLOADED member: vector insert/erase in
//     three arities, vector<double>, basic_string, a named iterator local, and the same shape on
//     a USER template (cppt.ConstIt) to show the rule is structural. Identity still outranks it,
//     a value/reference pair breaks on the argument rather than on declaration order, and
//     Test/errors/err_cpp_template_no_match.cb pins the three refusals (const removed, a
//     different pointee, and a constness-keyed partial specialization of differing layout).

import cpp "library/cpp_interop_basic.h" cache;
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_basic.cpp" cache;
// One header-only CLASS TEMPLATE pattern. No specialization has a symbol anywhere until a
// CFlat declaration asks for one, so every class-template assertion also proves the
// instantiation path emitted the bodies. The libc++ checks need no fixture at all - the
// libc++ headers are the fixture, reached by the SYSTEM header spelling below.
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_tpl.h" cache;
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_by_value.h" cache;
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_proxy.h" cache;
import cpp "vector" cache;
import cpp "tuple" cache;
import cpp "mutex" cache;
import cpp "chrono" cache;
import cpp "thread" cache;
import cpp "string" cache;
import cpp "algorithm" cache;
import cpp "memory" cache;
import cpp "numeric" cache;
import cpp "utility" cache;
import cpp "cstdlib" cache;
import cpp "cmath" cache;
import cpp "cstring" cache;
import cpp "cctype" cache;
import cpp "cstdio" cache;
import cpp "map" cache;
import cpp "atomic" cache;
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_scoped_enum.h" cache;
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_nsstd.h" cache;
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_strop.h" cache;
// std containers over std specializations over USER classes. Neither header
// includes a standard header, so no single group can declare both halves on its own.
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_nest.h" cache;
import cpp "library/cpp_interop_nest2.h" cache;

extern int strcmp(const char* a, const char* b);
// Class-template helper: the SAME specialization `cppt.Box<int>` a second function also declares. One
// registration and one emitted symbol have to serve both, or the link fails on a duplicate.
int tplbox_second_use(int v)
{
    cppt.Box<int> b = cppt.Box<int>(v);
    return b.get() + b[0];
}
// File-scope signature naming a scoped-enum NON-TYPE specialization: the ForwardRefScanner
// (ResolveForwardTypeArg) renders the argument here, the codegen pass renders it again.
int entnttp_take(cppi_scope.HueBox<cppi_scope.Hue.Red> value) { return value.get(); }
int qualtemp_take_box(cppt.Box<int> value) { return value.get(); }
int qualtemp_take_pair(cppt.CtorPair<int> value) { return value.first() + value.second(); }
int qualtemp_take_nested(cppt.Box<cppt.Box<int>> value) { return value.get().get(); }
int qualtemp_take_nested2(cppt.Box<cppt.Box<cppt.Box<int>>> value) { return value.get().get().get(); }
int qualtemp_take_payload(cppt.Box<cppt.impl_detail.Payload> value) { return value.get().get(); }
cppt.Box<int> qualtemp_return_box(int value) { return cppt.Box<int>(value); }
// Template-static helpers: the qualified C++ specialization spelling formed from a CFlat generic's own T.
T tplstaticTwiceStatic<T>(T value) { return cppt.TplStatics<T>.twice(value); }
int tplstaticRankStatic<T>() { return cppt.TplStatics<T>.rank(); }
// libc++ helper: a std.string built and read in a second function - the specialization is requested
// once for the whole compilation, not once per use site.
int libcxx_second_use()
{
    std.string s = std.string("abcd");
    return (int)s.size();
}
int stdfree_standard()
{
    std.vector<int> values = default;
    values.push_back(3); values.push_back(1); values.push_back(2);
    std.printf("stdfree-before-sort\n");
    std.sort(values.begin(), values.end());
    std.printf("stdfree-after-sort\n");
    if (values[0] != 1 || values[1] != 2 || values[2] != 3) return 1770;
    std.shared_ptr<int> shared = std.make_shared<int>(41);
    if (*shared != 41) return 1771;
    std.string text = std.to_string(42);
    if (text.size() != 2) return 1772;
    if (std.stoi(text) != 42) return 1773;
    if ((int)std.strlen("abcd") != 4) return 1774;

    int i = -7;
    double d = -2.5;
    long l = -9;
    if (std.abs(i) != 7) return 1775;
    if (std.abs(d) != 2.5) return 1776;
    if (std.abs(l) != 9) return 1777;
    if (std.sqrt(81.0) != 9.0) return 1778;
    if (std.max(3, 8) != 8) return 1779;
    if (std.max<int>(9, 2) != 9) return 1780;
    if (std.gcd(84, 30) != 6) return 1781;
    if (std.printf("") != 0) return 1782;
    if (std.toupper('a') != 65) return 1783;

    auto pair = std.make_pair(7, 9);
    if (pair.first != 7 || pair.second != 9) return 1784;
    auto started = std.chrono.steady_clock.now();
    std.chrono.duration<long long> delay = std.chrono.duration<long long>(1);
    std.this_thread.sleep_for(delay);
    auto finished = std.chrono.steady_clock.now();
    if (finished.time_since_epoch().count() <= started.time_since_epoch().count()) return 1785;
    if (delay.count() != 1) return 1786;
    return 0;
}

int stdfree_import_order()
{
    std.shared_ptr<int> shared = std.make_shared<int>(41);
    auto pair = std.make_pair(7, 9);
    if (*shared != 41 || pair.first != 7 || pair.second != 9) return 1787;
    return std.max<int>(9, 2) == 9 ? 0 : 1787;
}
// A CFlat-native operator[] whose index parameter is a struct. The subscript
// argument build is shared with the C++ path, so a struct index must keep its type here too.
struct KeyIdx { int v; };
struct KeyBag { int base; };
int operator[](KeyBag* bag, KeyIdx idx) { return bag->base + idx.v; }

struct KeyHolder { std.string name = default; };
int veciter_direct_array_param(std.array<int, 4> value)
{
    return cppi.array_total(value);
}
[cpp] struct AlnPatBase : alna.NBdef<int> { };

// A C++ alias template in a FILE-SCOPE CFlat signature: the parameter and return types are
// resolved by the ForwardRefScanner copy of the declaration path, not by the codegen copy.
int alnpat_take_nbdef(alna.NBdef<int> value) { return value.v + 100; }
alna.NBdef<int> alnpat_make_nbdef() { alna.NBdef<int> made = default; return made; }

/*
 * Section M103 helpers: a std container over a std specialization over a USER class, spelled in a
 * FILE-SCOPE SIGNATURE. These reach the type through the ForwardRefScanner's signature pre-pass,
 * which used to mangle a nested argument without ever requesting it - so the outer specialization
 * resolved in a <vector>+user-header group that cannot reach <memory> and the inner request
 * inherited that group and failed. The whole file is refused by the pre-fix binary right here,
 * with "'std::shared_ptr<nest::Cell>' does not name a C++ class type in the imported headers".
 */
int nestsig_param(std.vector<std.shared_ptr<nest.Cell>> v) { return (int)v.size(); }
// Returns EMPTY on purpose: returning a C++ class that already owns heap by value from a CFlat
// function aborts (SIGBUS), measured - that is the separate return-by-value copy family, not this
// fix. The leg below proves the returned object is usable rather than just counting zero.
std.vector<std.shared_ptr<nest.Cell>> nestsig_return()
{
    std.vector<std.shared_ptr<nest.Cell>> made = default;
    return made;
}
// Parameter AND return in one signature. It returns a FRESH empty vector whose capacity carries
// the parameter's size, rather than `return v;`: passing a by-value C++ class straight back out
// aborts in libc++ refcount teardown when other by-value legs are present - measured, and
// measured identically for std.vector<std.string> on the pre-fix binary (scratch/nsg_c1.cb, exit
// 133 both sides). That is the separate by-value C++ class copy family, not this fix.
std.vector<std.shared_ptr<nest.Cell>> nestsig_both(std.vector<std.shared_ptr<nest.Cell>> v)
{
    std.vector<std.shared_ptr<nest.Cell>> out = default;
    out.reserve((ulong)((int)v.size() + 4));
    return out;
}
// Depth 3.
int nestsig_depth3(std.vector<std.vector<std.shared_ptr<nest.Cell>>> v) { return (int)v.size(); }
// The inner user class taken from the SECOND user header instead.
int nestsig_group2(std.vector<std.shared_ptr<nest2.Tag>> v) { return (int)v.size(); }
// Declaration ORDER: this one is declared BEFORE any function that declares a local of the same
// spelling, so no earlier resolution can have cached the inner's owning group for it.
int nestsig_order_first(std.vector<std.shared_ptr<nest.Cell>> v) { return (int)v.size() + 100; }
int nestsig_order_seed()
{
    std.vector<std.shared_ptr<nest.Cell>> seeded = default;
    std.shared_ptr<nest.Cell> seed = default;
    seeded.push_back(seed);
    return (int)seeded.size();
}
// ... and this one AFTER that local, the order in which the cached resolution could mask the bug.
int nestsig_order_last(std.vector<std.shared_ptr<nest.Cell>> v) { return (int)v.size() + 200; }
// The same spelling as a FIELD of a file-scope CFlat struct (ForwardRefScanner struct-shell pass)
// and as the type ARGUMENT of a file-scope CFlat generic.
struct NestSigHolder
{
    std.vector<std.shared_ptr<nest.Cell>> items = default;
    int tag = 3;
};
struct NestSigBox<T>
{
    T item = default;
    int tag() { return 7; }
};
int nestsig_generic_param(NestSigBox<std.vector<std.shared_ptr<nest.Cell>>> b) { return b.tag(); }

// `return (*v)[0];` converts the std::vector<bool> element proxy under the ASSIGNMENT rules.
// Pre-fix this did not compile: "cannot return this value: its type does not match".
bool proxy_bool_return(std.vector<bool>* v)
{
    return (*v)[0];
}

// The same shape on the counted proxy: its temporary must be destroyed even though the caller
// receives only the converted bool. See leg 2380.
bool life_bool_return(LifeBag* b)
{
    return (*b)[0];
}

extern int main()
{
    // Win64 keeps the existing SEH trampoline and does not emit the C++ guard, so the
    // whole C++-interop surface is verified on the Itanium-ABI hosts only.
    if const (__WINDOWS__) {
        return 0;
    }

    // ---- class-typed subscript indices ----------------------------------------------------------
    // Runs early and in its own scope on purpose: internal/issue/p2/cpp-shared-ptr-vector-
    // stale-stack-control-block.md is a pre-existing stray write into main's frame.
    {
        // A named std.string lvalue as a std.map key. Pre-fix the index reached C++ member
        // overload matching as an unnamed aggregate value and no candidate bound.
        std.map<std.string, int> keyCounts = default;
        std.string keyString = std.string("compiler");
        keyCounts[keyString] = keyCounts[keyString] + 1;
        keyCounts[keyString] = keyCounts[keyString] + 1;
        if (keyCounts[keyString] != 2)                     return 1590;
        // One entry only: binding the by-value (key_type&&) leg instead of const key_type&
        // would move from keyString and the second subscript would insert a second, empty key.
        if ((int)keyCounts.size() != 1)                 return 1591;
        if (keyCounts["compiler"] != 2)                 return 1592;
        // The same named key through the members that already bound it before the fix.
        if ((int)keyCounts.count(keyString) != 1)          return 1593;
        auto keyFound = keyCounts.find(keyString);
        if (keyFound == keyCounts.end())                return 1594;
        // A struct FIELD and a DEREFERENCED POINTER are the other lvalue spellings.
        KeyHolder keyHolder = default;
        keyHolder.name = keyString;
        keyCounts[keyHolder.name] = keyCounts[keyHolder.name] + 3;
        if (keyCounts[keyHolder.name] != 5)             return 1595;
        std.string* keyPtr = &keyString;
        if (keyCounts[*keyPtr] != 5)                    return 1596;
        // A user-header C++ class key, and the same class through a const-reference
        // parameter - so the row is not std.string-specific.
        std.map<SubscriptKey, int> keyUser = default;
        SubscriptKey keyUserKey = SubscriptKey(3);
        keyUser[keyUserKey] = 8;
        if (keyUser[keyUserKey] != 8)                   return 1597;
        if (take_subscript_key(keyUserKey) != 4)              return 1598;
        // A CFlat-native operator[] taking a struct index shares the argument build.
        KeyBag keyBag = default;
        keyBag.base = 10;
        KeyIdx keyIdx = default;
        keyIdx.v = 4;
        if (keyBag[keyIdx] != 14)                       return 1599;
    }

    // ---- C++ class templates instantiated from CFlat --------------------------------------------
    // One header-only pattern, two specializations. Nothing below exists as a symbol until
    // these declarations ask for it.
    cppt.box_int_reset();
    {
        cppt.Box<int> tplboxB = cppt.Box<int>(7);
        if (tplboxB.get() != 7)                      return 480;   // constructor taking T
        if (cppt.box_int_live() != 1)            return 481;   // per-specialization static counter
        if (cppt.box_int_ctors() != 1)           return 482;
        tplboxB.set(9);
        if (tplboxB.get() != 9)                      return 483;   // mutating method taking T
        if (tplboxB[0] != 9)                         return 484;   // operator[] via the index expression
        cppt.Box<int> tplboxB2 = cppt.Box<int>(9);
        if (!(tplboxB == tplboxB2))                      return 485;   // operator== via the overload table
        cppt.Box<int> tplboxB3 = cppt.Box<int>(4);
        if (tplboxB == tplboxB3)                         return 486;
        if (cppt.box_int_live() != 3)            return 487;
    }
    if (cppt.box_int_live() != 0)                return 488;   // all three destroyed exactly once
    if (cppt.box_int_dtors() != 3)               return 489;

    // A SECOND specialization of the same pattern: its own instantiation, its own counter.
    {
        cppt.Box<double> tplboxD = cppt.Box<double>(2.5);
        if (tplboxD.get() != 2.5)                    return 490;
        if (tplboxD[0] != 2.5)                       return 491;
        if (cppt.box_double_live() != 1)         return 492;
        if (cppt.box_int_live() != 0)            return 493;   // counters are per specialization
    }
    if (cppt.box_double_live() != 0)             return 494;

    // The same specialization named in another function: one registration, one linked symbol.
    if (tplbox_second_use(5) != 10)                  return 495;
    if (cppt.box_int_live() != 0)                return 496;

    // A member can return a specialization that was not requested while its class was bound. The
    // first chained call must request LazyBox<int>, bind make_box, and then resolve get normally.
    {
        cppt.LazyBoxFactory tplboxLazy = default;
        if (tplboxLazy.make_box(3).get() != 3)        return 756;
        cppt.LazyBox<int> tplboxLazyBox = tplboxLazy.make_box(4);
        if (tplboxLazy.take_box(tplboxLazyBox) != 4)      return 757;
        // A local initialized from a CHAINED call (sret result move-constructed from the
        // statement temporary) and from a class the ABI returns in registers.
        cppt.LazyBox<int> tplboxChained = tplboxLazy.self().make_box(5);
        if (tplboxLazy.take_box(tplboxChained) != 5)      return 758;
        cppt.Slot tplboxSlot = tplboxLazy.make_slot(6);
        if (tplboxSlot.get() != 6)                    return 759;
        cppt.Slot tplboxSlot2 = tplboxLazy.self().make_slot(7);
        if (tplboxSlot2.get() != 7)                   return 760;
        cppi.Grid tplboxGrid = default;
        if (tplboxGrid.sum() != 10)                   return 761;
        cppi.Earlier tplboxEarly = default;
        tplboxEarly.a = 5;
        cppi.Later tplboxLater = tplboxEarly.to_later();
        if (tplboxLater.sum() != 18)                  return 762;
        cppi.Later tplboxLater2 = (cppi.Later)tplboxEarly;
        if (tplboxLater2.sum() != 15)                 return 763;
        cppt.via_alias.Payload tplboxPayload = default;
        // The canonical spelling first, so the alias spelling below must alias onto it.
